"7.14": {
"deck": 7,
"n": 14,
"texts": [
"Results",
"General observations Sufficient to good internal consistencies. Pre-intervention Positive, interrelated, attitudes about the use of Virtual Reality. Willingness associated positively with immersion & usefulness. Assessment Significant improvement from pre-test to post-test (theory). Almost 1 in 2 was correct on first attempt on all practical aspects (VR). No associations between theoretical and practical knowledge. Post-intervention Overly positive stance over the educational Virtual Reality workshop. Immersion, enjoyment, usefulness & realism positively associated with each other. Realism influenced attractiveness but reflected the perception of greater content difficulty."
],
